{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T15:46:40.576Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"b2ed10cbfe9ede2fb711f0a0","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-review-2jcx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Changelog gate fails silently on drift: print the drift classification and diff"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The deep tier's changelog:check (scripts/changelog.ts --check) exits 1 with no output at all when the committed changelog is out of date, because the wrapper compared the generated markdown with the committed file itself and returned 1 without a message. The scheduled deep legs then failed with nothing but an exit code. Delegate the check verdict to the generator's own --check path, which prints the drift classification and a unified diff, so a failing gate explains itself. The underlying drift in the observed deep failure was a release-tag race: a queued deep run audits a pre-release snapshot while the release tag already exists, and the generator rebuilds full history from every tag; that reachability scoping belongs upstream (pm item for the follow-up)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-23T15:46:40.576Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T15:46:40.576Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex-agent"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"cd0bb0f01b210c9733eca0fa24f87527e1c844c26202aa4b6b09644b9f