{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T15:46:53.667Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"b2ed10cbfe9ede2fb711f0a0","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T15:46:53.667Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-23T15:46:53.667Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Classification (scheduled-failure triage 2026-11-23, deep run 44715927320): class 1. All four deep legs failed 'Full npm release gate'/'Full Bun release gate' at changelog:check with exit code 1 and NO output. Reproduced locally at the failing commit: the committed changelog still carried an 'Unreleased' section while the generator, rebuilding full history from every release tag, produced the released '2026.11.20' section (the v2026.11.20 tag landed at 12:59Z, after the run's 10:03Z snapshot) - a queued-snapshot release-tag race; current main passes because the release commit regenerated the changelog. The in-repo defect this PR fixes: the wrapper's own byte compare returned 1 without any message, so the deep legs failed silently. Fix: forward --check to the generator and return its verdict, so the gate prints the drift classification and unified diff through the generator's own check path."}]}],"before_hash":"59b16599d4d16be090e0410aeb7f50689f2f2f7c423b2cc66dbd69a14aaeeeb1","after_hash":"855b57a5147895deb3680ade5548c3304201f17ee78209f434bc530eabbd25c6","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"818391f24e10b710544fee3631bacf40d6d327a7465c2eb66da9b62840397921"}
